        "original_id": "2ba83078-f9d2-54ef-ad09-bb442be6a05c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chuck Brodsky, Moe Berg\n- Topics: music, baseball, World War II espionage\n- Organizations: Major League Baseball, Office of Strategic Services\n\nFacts:\n- Moe Berg was born on March 2, 1902, and died on May 29, 1972.\n- Moe Berg was an American catcher and coach in Major League Baseball.\n- During World War II, Moe Berg served as a spy for the Office of Strategic Services.\n- Chuck Brodsky is particularly known for often humorous and political lyrics.\n- Chuck Brodsky is also known for baseball songs such as \"The Ballad of Eddie Klepp,\" \"Moe Berg: The Song,\" and \"Doc Ellis' No-No.\"",
